## Binding Behaviour

**Do not run a skill that belongs to a later phase than the current one.**
When asked to, say which phase the work belongs to, which phase the product is
in, and what would have to be approved first. Then offer to do the current
phase's work instead.

**Never mark a gate approved on the user's behalf.** `approve` requires
`--by "name"`. A gate a machine can clear is not a gate. Recording a review
verdict with `record-gate` is the agent's job; granting approval is not.

**Never review your own phase.** Run `lifecycle.mjs gate PHASE` and launch the
reviewer it names as a fresh subagent. If you wrote any of the artifacts, you are
the wrong reader for them no matter how carefully you read.

**Never propose an override.** There is no `--force`. A bypass is an `override`
record with an owner, a risk level and an expiry, and it exists for a human who
has decided to accept a specific risk. An agent suggesting one is the failure the
gate was built to prevent.

**Never soften a gate failure.** Same rule as `/production-readiness-review`:
a gate that has never blocked anything is a form, not a control.

**The write policy is enforced, not requested.** `guard-phase.mjs` returns exit
code 2 on any write the current phase does not permit. The policy is data, in
`.cursor/lifecycle/write-policy.json`:

| Artifact | Earliest phase | Needs cleared |
|---|---|---|
| `src/`, `backend/`, `frontend/` source | DEVELOPMENT | DESIGN |
| Database migrations | DEVELOPMENT | DESIGN |
| IaC — `*.tf`, `*.bicep`, `infra/` | DESIGN | ANALYSIS |
| CI pipelines — `.github/workflows/` | TESTING | DEVELOPMENT |
| Deployment manifests — `k8s/`, `helm/` | PRODUCTION | TESTING |

`earliest: X` means the phase **before** X must be `APPROVED` or `INHERITED` —
`STALE` included, so an edited design document re-blocks source on the next call.

Never blocked: `tests/`, `specs/`, `docs/`, `memory-bank/`, `.cursor/`,
`.claude/`, `*.md`. Writing a test or a spec early is good practice, not a
violation. If it blocks you,
stop and tell the user why. Do not route around it with `Bash`.

Tests, specs, docs and `memory-bank/` are never blocked — writing a test or a
spec before the design gate is good practice, not a violation.

